('MPM2D', 'quadratics', 'factored-form-and-zeros', 19, 'Challenge',
 'A parabola in standard form is y = x² - 9. Find its x-intercepts by factoring.', 3,
 '[{"text": "x = 9 and x = -9", "feedback": "This treats 9 as if it were the roots directly — factor x²-9 as a difference of squares first."}, {"text": "x = 3 only", "feedback": "A parabola with two distinct x-intercepts crosses the x-axis twice — x²-9 factors into two different linear factors."}, {"text": "x = 81", "feedback": "This squares 9 instead of taking its square root — x²-9 is a difference of squares, x²-3²."}, {"text": "x = 3 and x = -3", "feedback": "Correct. x²-9 is a difference of squares, factoring as (x-3)(x+3); setting each factor to 0 gives x=3 and x=-3."}]'::jsonb,
