('MPM2D', 'trigonometry', 'cosine-law', 10, 'Easy',
 'True or false: every equilateral triangle is an acute triangle.', 0,
 '[{"text": "True", "feedback": "Correct. An equilateral triangle''s three angles are always equal, and since they sum to 180°, each one is exactly 60° — well under 90°, making it acute."}, {"text": "False, because equilateral triangles have no defined angles", "feedback": "Every triangle, equilateral or not, has three well-defined interior angles that sum to 180°."}, {"text": "False, because equilateral triangles are always right triangles", "feedback": "A right triangle needs one angle of exactly 90° — an equilateral triangle''s angles are all 60°, nowhere near 90°."}, {"text": "It depends on the side lengths", "feedback": "An equilateral triangle''s angles are always 60°-60°-60°, regardless of how long its sides are — so it''s always acute."}]'::jsonb,
